#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
berth — the dev workspace as a berth: who is moored here, what they hold, what they said.

This is the local, ephemeral slice of a protocol shape, not a new invention. In tevah terms the
workspace container is ONE berth (a blade with declared carrying capacity: RAM, disk-write budget,
CPU, one household mesh, one heavy cargo slot). Sessions — Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity, a
human at a terminal — MOOR to it, CLAIM capacity, RELEASE it, and SAY things to each other while
they deliberate. Every record here is written in the field shape of its eventual protocol home so
projection is a rename, never a redesign:

  mooring   → a `delegates-compute` Mishpat::Commitment  (provider = the human principal,
              recipient = the agent {model, lab, runtime, session}, bounds = {write_set, ttl});
              see genesis/docs/architecture/rea-compute-commitment-primitive.md
  lease     → a REA commitment to `use` one unit of a berth resource for a bounded window
              (tevah §5.3 "Commitment (before)"); a refused claim is an honest absence, not a queue
  note      → a witnessed interaction event between moored agents (low stakes ⇒ never notarized)
  shed      → tevah §5.3 "breach event", written here by io-guard / ram-guard when they act

Classification (p2p-design-gate, 2026-09-03): every record is Ephemeral (C) — delete the store and
it is rebuilt from the live processes and the next moor/claim. Source of truth: the running
workspace. Store: $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/berth (survives container restarts; never inside /tmp; never
in git). Design note: genesis/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-workspace-berth-carrying-capacity-design.md

Commands:
  berth moor    --session S [--model M] [--lab L] [--runtime R] [--principal P] [--task T]
                [--writes a,b,c] [--pid N] [--ttl SECONDS]         register / refresh this session
  berth unmoor  --session S                                        leave; releases every lease held
  berth touch   --session S [--pid N]                              liveness heartbeat (hooks call it)
  berth claim   RESOURCE --session S [--class verify|measure|mesh] [--ttl SECONDS] [--note TEXT]
                [--closure KEY] [--offline-ok]                      take one unit; exit 3 if held or refused
  berth release RESOURCE --session S [--force]                     --force gives back whoever holds it
  berth owner-check RESOURCE [--action A] [--force]                exit 3 while another live session
                                                                   holds it; --force = override row
  berth say     --session S [--to SESSION] TEXT                    a deliberation note; the addressee reads
                                                                   it with `berth inbox` or watches `--follow`
  berth inbox   --session S [--peek] [--all] [--follow] [--json]  read notes said to this session
  berth who     RESOURCE                                           json of the holder (or null)
  berth status                                                     moorings · leases · capacity, and the
                                                                   other devices' moorings and steward
                                                                   leases, read from this device's fold
  berth ledger  [-n 30]                                            the append-only record
  berth reap                                                       remove dead expired moorings and expired leases
  berth overrun-check [RESOURCE]                                   emit dev-berth-held-by-measure@1 once
                                                                   for a lease held past its ttl (hooks)

Resources (capacity 1 unless pool-policy.json `berth.resources` says otherwise):
  mesh        the household mesh (start/stop/prologue/test mesh)
  cargo       one heavy cargo build/test/check per container (pool-policy io.max_concurrent_heavy)
  disk-heavy  any sustained-write job that is not cargo (prologue seed, pnpm install, blob sync)

Steward-scoped resources (pool-policy.json `berth.resources.<name>.scope: steward`) are shared by every
device of one person, not this workspace alone: dev-integration, jenkins-dispatch, alpha-fleet and every
`lane:<id>`. A claim on one writes its lease (a crossing record), then reads `epr peer leases --json`
every 250 ms until the verdict leaves pending, at most `berth.channel.confirm_wait_s` (10 s): it is
effective once every other admitted device has acknowledged it and the holder fence has a recent
head covering its latest renew, at once when no other device is admitted. A fenced renewal stays
recorded but self-demotes and exits non-zero. A refused claim releases with one reason line:
  held by <device-did>/<session> since <YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ>
  unconfirmed: <device-did> last seen <n>s|<n>m|<n>h ago   (or: never seen)
--offline-ok writes a `kind: override` row naming the silent device; the lease remains unconfirmed
until ttl + max skew + fence margin after that device was last seen, and a no-ttl lease never becomes
effective by override. It never overrides `held by`. `owner-check` reads the same view. A missing
`epr` or a view it cannot compute refuses: an absent device is never read as a free resource.
Container-scoped resources never ask a peer.

Lease classes (pool-policy.json `berth.classes.<resource>`; a resource with no table takes any class
and gets no default ttl). The mesh lease is the dev berth's router:
  verify   a bounded lane (`just test mesh`): default ttl 1800 s, a ttl above max_ttl_s (3600) is
           refused — a longer hold is a measure, and says so
  measure  a window/A-B/soak/proof run: REFUSED here (exit 3) with its alternative, `just measure
           <scope>` on a measurement peer. MEASURE_ON_DEV_BERTH=1 with --ttl declares an override:
           it claims, writes a `kind: override` row and emits dev-berth-held-by-measure@1 = ttl at once
  mesh     the DAEMON lease — the household being up (`just mesh start`): no ttl, never taken over by
           expiry, only when its holder's mooring is dead. A lane the holder runs under it is covered;
           any other class change on a held lease is refused (release, then claim)
A lease carries class · ttl_s · claimed_at · holder · seat (the REA `use` commitment's fields).
A mooring's runtime-asserted pid carries its incarnation (`pid_start`, /proc stat field 22): a live pid
with a different start time is a dead mooring. `claimed_at` is set once; a renew (the holder claiming again) resets `since` only, is on the record
as a `renew` row carrying $BERTH_SEAT, and cannot carry the hold past the class's max_ttl_s without
an explicit --ttl, which is itself capped.

Session id resolution: an explicit fixture/operator flag, else the shared P1 shim. No berth-specific
ancestry or runtime environment key participates. A mooring expires
`ttl` seconds after its last touch (pool-policy `berth.mooring_ttl_s`, default 3 h); a lease expires
`ttl_s` after its last claim or renew. An expired lease can be taken over, and the takeover is on the
record with `expired_after_s`. Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 a renew, release or unmoor done here whose record
did not reach this device's channel store (named; the other devices still hold the earlier terms), or a
note said here that no other device will read · 2 usage · 3 refused (held by a live mooring, a class
this berth does not run, a ttl past the class's cap, a class transition, an owner check) · 4 no session
resolvable (or ambiguous), or the store itself cannot be opened (a guest sandbox: EACCES/ENOENT on
the lock or dir) — the only code a wrapper may proceed past, unleased.
"""
import contextlib
import errno
import fcntl
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import time

CONFIG_DIR = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR", "/projects/.claude-config")
PROJECT_DIR = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR", "/projects/elohim")
POLICY_FILE = os.path.join(PROJECT_DIR, "genesis", "agentic", "pool-policy.json")
DEFAULT_TTL_S = 3 * 3600
DEFAULT_RESOURCES = {"mesh": 1, "cargo": 1, "disk-heavy": 1}
DEFAULT_CLASS = "verify"
DEFAULT_CONFIRM_WAIT_S = 10
DEFAULT_FRESHNESS_S = 90
DEFAULT_FENCE_MARGIN_S = 30
DEFAULT_MAX_SKEW_S = 30
POLL_S = 1.0  # how often a steward claim re-reads the lease view (each read parses the whole flow store)
PEER_TIMEOUT_S = 10
OVERRUN_MEASURE = "dev-berth-held-by-measure@1"
EVENTS_MEASURE = "dev-berth-events@1"
# The berth record kinds that cross to the steward's other devices (pool-policy berth.channel.crosses).
CROSSING_KINDS = ("moor", "unmoor", "claim", "renew", "release", "override", "note", "shed")
# A session's mooring crosses with its steward leases, so the other devices can list who is moored here.
MOORING_KINDS = ("moor", "unmoor")
# The measure emitter lives beside the hooks; bin/berth → genesis/agentic → genesis → repo root.
REPO_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))))
HOOKS_DIR = os.path.join(REPO_ROOT, ".claude", "hooks")
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(REPO_ROOT, ".claude", "scripts"))
from _lib.session import resolve as resolve_session_identity

def _predates_envelopes(result):
    """Whether `epr session prepare-berth` was answered by a build older than envelopes.

    A build with no `session` verb refuses it by name; slice A's `session` knew only `id` and
    printed that usage with exit 0 for any other verb.
    """
    if result.returncode:
        return "unknown command `session`" in result.stderr
    return result.stdout.startswith("epr session id")


@contextlib.contextmanager
def envelope_guard(session, berth_store):
    """Hold the native lifecycle flock across mutations, including direct Berth callers.

    Native validation owns the binding and closure predicates. Standalone berth stores
    without a device retain their existing behavior. Initialize before taking the lock.
    """
    key = os.environ.get("ELOHIM_DEVICE_KEY_FILE")
    config = os.environ.get("XDG_CONFIG_HOME", "")
    if not key:
        config = config if os.path.isabs(config) else os.path.expanduser("~/.config")
        key = os.path.join(config, "elohim/device/ed25519.seed")
    directory = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(key), "sessions")
    if not os.path.isdir(directory) and not os.path.isfile(key):
        yield
        return
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(
            [os.environ.get("EPR_BIN") or "epr", "session", "prepare-berth",
             "--session", session, "--store", os.path.realpath(berth_store)],
            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        result = None  # no `epr` at all: it cannot have opened an envelope either
    if result is None or _predates_envelopes(result):
        # A session runs only its pinned `epr`, and only an envelope-capable `epr` can open an
        # envelope, so a session pinned to an older build has none and no close can race this
        # mutation. Sessions keep their pins across a landing, so this is every live session on a
        # device the moment envelopes land.
        yield
        return
    if result.returncode:
        raise BerthUsage(result.stderr.strip() or "envelope preparation failed")
    with open(os.path.join(directory, ".lock"), "a") as lock:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_SH)
        result = subprocess.run(
            [os.environ.get("EPR_BIN") or "epr", "session", "validate", "--session", session],
            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
        if result.returncode:
            raise BerthUsage(result.stderr.strip() or "envelope validation failed")
        yield


# The checkout this berth lives in, fixed at load (tests may repoint REPO_ROOT; this never moves).
HOME_CHECKOUT = REPO_ROOT
# Set by berth_test for its own process and every berth it spawns: under the test runner the real
# emitter never folds into this berth's own checkout (a suite run once grew it by 13,000 test records).
UNDER_TEST_ENV = "BERTH_UNDER_TEST"


# The line a refusal adds when the claim is unconfirmed while this device's own daemon is down: the
# other device was never told, so the cure is here, not there.
DAEMON_DOWN_LINE = "(this device's peer daemon is not running: start it with epr peer serve)"
# A failed `epr` call whose first line says "unknown command" or "usage:": a binary built before
# `epr peer` existed. `{path}` is that binary.
STALE_EPR_HINT = ("{path} predates the peer verbs: replace it (epr device arrive installs the native launcher "
                  "onto PATH) or export EPR_BIN=<a current epr>")

class BerthUsage(ValueError):
    """A claim the caller mis-stated (unknown class, override without a ttl) — exit 2, no record."""


class BerthAmbiguous(LookupError):
    """Two live moorings share this process's nearest moored ancestor — exit 4, never a guess."""


EXIT_NO_SESSION = 4  # no session resolvable (or ambiguous): callers may proceed unleased; 2 = usage


def pid_alive(pid):
    try:
        os.kill(int(pid), 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except PermissionError:
        pass
    except (ValueError, OSError):
        return False
    return True


def pid_start_time(pid):
    """The process's start time (clock ticks since boot, /proc/<pid>/stat field 22) — the incarnation
    a pid alone cannot name. None when unreadable."""
    try:
        with open(f"/proc/{int(pid)}/stat") as f:
            return int(f.read().rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()[19])
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        return None


def write_json_atomic(path, obj):
    """Publish a whole file or nothing: a reader never sees a half-written mooring or lease table."""
    tmp = f"{path}.{os.getpid()}.tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(obj, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def store_dir():
    return os.environ.get("BERTH_DIR") or os.path.join(CONFIG_DIR, "berth")


def main_checkout(root):
    """A linked worktree's main checkout, without relying on the hook's exported Git context.
    A separate git dir or submodule is not a main checkout; keep the supplied root there."""
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(root, ".git")) as f:
            marker = f.read().strip()
        if not marker.startswith("gitdir: "):
            return root
        git_dir = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(root, marker[8:]))
        with open(os.path.join(git_dir, "commondir")) as f:
            common = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(git_dir, f.read().strip()))
        if os.path.basename(common) == ".git" and os.path.isdir(common):
            return os.path.dirname(common)
    except OSError:
        pass
    return root


def load_policy(path=POLICY_FILE):
    """(capacities, mooring_ttl_s, classes) from pool-policy.json; defaults on any miss."""
    caps = dict(DEFAULT_RESOURCES)
    mooring_ttl_s = DEFAULT_TTL_S
    classes = {}
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            pol = json.load(f)
        io_pol = pol.get("io") or {}
        if "max_concurrent_heavy" in io_pol:
            caps["cargo"] = int(io_pol["max_concurrent_heavy"])
        berth = pol.get("berth") or {}
        for k, v in (berth.get("resources") or {}).items():
            if k.startswith("_"):
                continue
            caps[k] = int(v.get("capacity", 1)) if isinstance(v, dict) else int(v)
        if berth.get("mooring_ttl_s"):
            mooring_ttl_s = int(berth["mooring_ttl_s"])
        classes = {k: v for k, v in (berth.get("classes") or {}).items() if isinstance(v, dict)}
    except Exception:
        pass
    return caps, mooring_ttl_s, classes


def load_capacities(path=POLICY_FILE):
    return load_policy(path)[0]


def load_steward(path=POLICY_FILE):
    """(names, prefixes, confirm_wait_s, freshness_s, fence_margin_s, max_skew_s, error): the steward-scoped resources
    pool-policy.json declares (`berth.resources.<name>.scope: steward`; a key ending in `:` is a
    prefix) and the channel's waits. An absent file declares none. A file that does not parse, or an
    entry that is neither a capacity nor `{capacity, scope: container|steward}`, is an `error`: the
    policy can then not say which resources are shared, so every claim refuses naming it."""
    names, prefixes = set(), set()
    wait, fresh = DEFAULT_CONFIRM_WAIT_S, DEFAULT_FRESHNESS_S
    margin, skew = DEFAULT_FENCE_MARGIN_S, DEFAULT_MAX_SKEW_S
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            berth = json.load(f).get("berth") or {}
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return names, prefixes, wait, fresh, margin, skew, None
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError) as e:
        return names, prefixes, wait, fresh, margin, skew, f"{path} does not parse: {e}"
    try:
        for k, v in (berth.get("resources") or {}).items():
            if k.startswith("_") or isinstance(v, int):
                continue
            if not isinstance(v, dict):
                raise ValueError(f"berth.resources.{k} is neither a capacity nor an object")
            scope = v.get("scope", "container")
            if scope not in ("container", "steward"):
                raise ValueError(f"berth.resources.{k} has unknown scope {scope!r} (container | steward)")
            if scope == "steward":
                (prefixes if k.endswith(":") else names).add(k)
        channel = berth.get("channel") or {}
        wait = int(channel.get("confirm_wait_s", wait))
        fresh = int(channel.get("freshness_s", fresh))
        margin = int(channel.get("fence_margin_s", margin))
        skew = int(channel.get("max_skew_s", skew))
    except (AttributeError, TypeError, ValueError) as e:
        return set(), set(), wait, fresh, margin, skew, f"{path}: {e}"
    return names, prefixes, wait, fresh, margin, skew, None


def _rfc3339(ms):
    """Unix milliseconds as RFC 3339 UTC, whole seconds (floored), `Z`."""
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(int(ms) // 1000))


def _peer_age(ms):
    """An age for a refusal line: `<n>s` under 120 s, `<n>m` under 120 min, else `<n>h` (floored)."""
    secs = max(0, int(ms) // 1000)
    return f"{secs}s" if secs < 120 else (f"{secs // 60}m" if secs < 7200 else f"{secs // 3600}h")


def steward_reason(verdict, now_ms, fence_after_s=None):
    """The one reason line a refused steward claim prints, from its `epr peer leases` verdict:
    `held by <device>/<session> since <time>` or `unconfirmed: <device> last seen <age> ago`. The a2o
    steps for devices-share-one-berth match these words; this is their only formatter."""
    if verdict.get("verdict") == "held_by":
        return f"held by {verdict['device']}/{verdict['session']} since {_rfc3339(verdict['since'])}"
    if verdict.get("verdict") == "refused_by":
        return f"refused by {verdict['device']}"
    if verdict.get("fenced"):
        window = f" within {fence_after_s}s" if fence_after_s is not None else " recently"
        return f"self-demoted: no head from {verdict['device']}{window}"
    if verdict.get("override_at") is not None:
        return (f"unconfirmed: {verdict['device']} — override effective at "
                f"{_rfc3339(verdict['override_at'])}")
    seen = verdict.get("last_seen")
    if seen is None:
        return f"unconfirmed: {verdict['device']} never seen"
    return f"unconfirmed: {verdict['device']} last seen {_peer_age(now_ms - seen)} ago"



def _safe(name):
    return "".join(c if c.isalnum() or c in "_.-" else "_" for c in str(name))


class Berth:
    def __init__(self, d=None, now=None, obs=None, policy_path=POLICY_FILE):
        self.dir = d or store_dir()
        self.moor_dir = os.path.join(self.dir, "moorings")
        os.makedirs(self.moor_dir, exist_ok=True)
        self.leases_path = os.path.join(self.dir, "leases.json")
        self.ledger_path = os.path.join(self.dir, "ledger.jsonl")
        self.lock_path = os.path.join(self.dir, "berth.lock")
        self.emitted_dir = os.path.join(self.dir, "emitted")
        self.now = now or time.time
        self.policy_path = policy_path
        self.capacities, self.mooring_ttl_s, self.classes = load_policy(policy_path)
        (self.steward_names, self.steward_prefixes,
         self.confirm_wait_s, self.freshness_s, self.fence_margin_s,
         self.max_skew_s, self.policy_error) = load_steward(policy_path)
        self.epr = None  # injectable: the `epr` a steward claim asks; else resolved like the fold emitter
        # The device's channel store (`epr peer leases` names it): steward records are written there,
        # so they cross. None until the view was read, or when this workspace is not a device.
        self.channel_root = None
        self.channel_standing = None
        self.channel_error = None
        self._channel_read = False
        self.fold_failures = []  # (resource, kind, why): steward records that did not reach the channel store
        self.sleep = time.sleep  # injectable: tests advance a fake clock instead
        self._obs = obs  # the `_observation` emitter; injected by tests, else imported lazily
        self._obs_injected = obs is not None
        self._lock_depth = {}
        self._pending_folds = []  # (kind, row) queued by record(); flushed once no berth lock is held
        self.pid_alive = pid_alive  # injectable: tests model liveness and incarnation
        self.pid_start = pid_start_time

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ records
    def _moor_path(self, session):
        return os.path.join(self.moor_dir, f"{_safe(session)}.json")

    @contextlib.contextmanager
    def _locked(self, name="berth"):
        """One writer at a time. `berth` serializes the ledger append and every read-modify-write of
        leases.json and the moorings (ram-guard's heartbeat goes through `touch`, so it is under it
        too); `emit` serializes the once-per-lease pain check so two prompt-triggered checks cannot
        both emit, without holding the claim path hostage to an `epr` subprocess. Re-entrant per
        name within this object (claim → record), because a second flock on a fresh open file
        description in the same process would wait on itself."""
        if self._lock_depth.get(name):
            self._lock_depth[name] += 1
            try:
                yield
            finally:
                self._lock_depth[name] -= 1
            return
        path = self.lock_path if name == "berth" else os.path.join(self.dir, f"{name}.lock")
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_CREAT | os.O_RDWR, 0o644)
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
            self._lock_depth[name] = 1
            try:
                yield
            finally:
                self._lock_depth[name] = 0
                fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
        finally:
            os.close(fd)
        if name == "berth":
            self._flush_folds()  # outermost exit: the lock is released, the `epr` subprocess may run

    def record(self, kind, **fields):
        with self._locked():
            # `dseq` is this device's record counter: it orders the device's records for the other
            # devices, which a step of this device's clock (`at`) cannot.
            ev = {"at": round(self.now(), 3), "kind": kind, "dseq": self._next_dseq()}
            ev.update(fields)
            line = (json.dumps(ev, sort_keys=True) + "\n").encode()
            fd = os.open(self.ledger_path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_APPEND | os.O_CREAT, 0o644)
            try:
                os.write(fd, line)
            finally:
                os.close(fd)
        # Queue, never emit under the lock: record() runs inside claim/release/moor's critical section
        # (the lock is re-entrant), and a slow `epr` (5 s timeout) would stall every concurrent claimant.
        # The queue flushes when the outermost `berth` lock exits — here, if record() is the outermost.
        # External writers (io-guard's shed rows) must go through Berth.record so they fold too.
        self._pending_folds.append((kind, ev))
        if not self._lock_depth.get("berth"):
            self._flush_folds()
        return ev

    def _next_dseq(self):
        """The next record number of this device (the berth lock is held). Persisted in the berth dir —
        one per container, so every worktree's berth shares it — before it is used, so it is never
        reused. A lost counter resumes above every number this device has written: its ledger, and its
        own records in its flow stores (never another device's, folded via it)."""
        path = os.path.join(self.dir, "dseq")
        try:
            with open(path) as f:
                last = int(f.read().strip())
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            last = self._highest_dseq()
        n = last + 1
        tmp = f"{path}.{os.getpid()}.tmp"
        with open(tmp, "w") as f:
            f.write(f"{n}\n")
            f.flush()
            os.fsync(f.fileno())
        os.replace(tmp, path)
        return n

    def dseq_stores(self):
        """The checkouts whose flow stores hold this device's own records: this checkout and, on a
        device, its channel store — asked of `epr peer leases` when not yet known (a lost berth dir),
        since that is where its steward records and moorings went."""
        if (not self.channel_root and not self._channel_read and (self.steward_names or self.steward_prefixes)
                and self.epr_bin()):
            self.peer_leases()
        roots = [REPO_ROOT, self.channel_root or self.cached_channel_root()]
        return list(dict.fromkeys(root for root in roots if root))

    def _channel_cache_path(self):
        return os.path.join(self.dir, "channel-store")

    def cached_channel_root(self):
        """The channel store the last view of this device named (the berth dir is one per container,
        so every worktree's berth shares it), or None."""
        try:
            with open(self._channel_cache_path()) as f:
                return f.read().strip() or None
        except OSError:
            return None

    def _remember_channel(self, root):
        """Keep where this device's channel store is, so a later berth process folds its moorings
        there without asking `epr` first; forget it once the workspace is not a device."""
        path = self._channel_cache_path()
        try:
            if root is None:
                os.remove(path)
            elif self.cached_channel_root() != root:
                tmp = f"{path}.{os.getpid()}.tmp"
                with open(tmp, "w") as f:
                    f.write(root + "\n")
                os.replace(tmp, path)
        except OSError:
            pass

    def _highest_dseq(self):
        highest = 0
        for ev in self.ledger(0):
            if isinstance(ev.get("dseq"), int):
                highest = max(highest, ev["dseq"])
        pattern = re.compile(r'"env:dseq=(\d+)"')
        for root in self.dseq_stores():
            try:
                with open(os.path.join(root, ".eprfs", "status", "flows.jsonl"), encoding="utf-8",
                          errors="replace") as f:
                    for line in f:
                        if "env:dseq=" not in line or '"via:' in line:
                            continue
                        for found in pattern.findall(line):
                            highest = max(highest, int(found))
            except OSError:
                continue
        return highest

    def _flush_folds(self):
        while self._pending_folds:
            kind, ev = self._pending_folds.pop(0)
            self._fold(kind, ev)

    def _fold(self, kind, ev):
        """The same record as one `dev-berth-events@1` fold on this host's flow store (habit
        ledgers-fold-once). Subject is always `.`: `epr flow note` resolves a subject as an atom address,
        gap id or readable path and refuses a bare resource name like `cargo`, so the resource rides in
        env (as in dev-berth-held-by-measure@1). reason = the kind; env = every field of the record as a
        string (absent fields omitted; lists/dicts as compact JSON; a row's own `reason` rides as env:reason,
        distinct from the emit's --reason = the kind). Called only from _flush_folds, i.e. with no berth
        lock held. Fail-open for this checkout's own records: a missing emitter costs the fold, never the
        lease. A steward-scoped record of a device that does not reach its channel store is not silent:
        it is kept in `fold_failures` for the claim, renew or release that wrote it to report."""
        resource = ev.get("resource")
        steward = isinstance(resource, str) and self.steward_scoped(resource)
        root, unreachable = self._fold_root(ev)
        if unreachable:
            self._fold_failed(kind, ev, unreachable)
            return False
        try:
            obs = self.observation()
            if obs is None or self._fold_refused_under_test(root):
                landed = False
            else:
                env = {}
                for k, v in ev.items():
                    if v is None:
                        continue
                    env[k] = v if isinstance(v, str) else (
                        json.dumps(v, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":")) if isinstance(v, (list, dict)) else str(v))
                landed = bool(obs.emit(EVENTS_MEASURE, ".", 1, reason=kind, env=env, root=root))
        except Exception:
            landed = False
        # A note bound for the channel store is a crossing record too: one the emitter could not write
        # (no `epr` resolved, a refusal) stays in this berth's ledger, where no other device reads it.
        crossing = steward or (kind == "note" and resource is None)
        if not landed and crossing and self.channel_root and root == self.channel_root:
            self._fold_failed(kind, ev, "`epr flow note` did not write it")
        return landed

    def _fold_refused_under_test(self, root):
        """Under the test runner ($BERTH_UNDER_TEST=1), the real emitter never writes into the checkout
        this berth lives in or its main checkout: a test record is not this workspace's record.
        An injected emitter, or a scratch checkout, is unaffected."""
        if os.environ.get(UNDER_TEST_ENV) != "1" or self._obs_injected or not root:
            return False
        # The checkout this file lives in, fixed at load: a test that repoints REPO_ROOT at a
        # scratch checkout folds there.
        return os.path.realpath(root) in (os.path.realpath(HOME_CHECKOUT), main_checkout(HOME_CHECKOUT))

    def _fold_failed(self, kind, ev, why):
        if kind in CROSSING_KINDS:
            where = self.channel_root or "its location unknown"
            self.fold_failures.append((ev.get("resource"), kind,
                                       f"the {kind} record did not reach this device's channel store ({where}): {why}"))

    def take_fold_failures(self, resource):
        """The crossing records about `resource` that did not reach the channel store, cleared."""
        mine = [why for res, _, why in self.fold_failures if res == resource]
        self.fold_failures = [f for f in self.fold_failures if f[0] != resource]
        return mine

    def take_release_fold_failures(self):
        """(resource, why) for every release record that did not reach the channel store, cleared."""
        mine = [(res, why) for res, kind, why in self.fold_failures if kind == "release"]
        self.fold_failures = [f for f in self.fold_failures if f[1] != "release"]
        return mine

    def _fold_root(self, ev):
        """(root, unreachable): where a record folds. Notes and steward-scoped resource records go to
        the device's channel store (the one `epr peer serve` projects), so they cross; everything else, and
        every record of a workspace that is not one of its steward's devices, to this checkout. A
        device whose channel store cannot be read gets no root, never this checkout's in its place."""
        resource = ev.get("resource")
        if ev.get("kind") in MOORING_KINDS and resource is None:
            # A mooring crosses when this workspace is a device whose channel store is known (this
            # process read it, or an earlier one did), and never fails. Only a worktree with nothing
            # known yet asks `epr` once, because its own store is never the one served: a device
            # admitted minutes ago would otherwise moor where no peer can see it.
            root = self.channel_root or self.cached_channel_root()
            if not root and not self._channel_read and main_checkout(REPO_ROOT) != REPO_ROOT:
                self.peer_leases()
                root = self.channel_root
            return root or REPO_ROOT, None
        note = (ev.get("kind") == "note" and resource is None
                and bool(self.steward_names or self.steward_prefixes))
        if not (note or isinstance(resource, str) and self.steward_scoped(resource)):
            return REPO_ROOT, None
        if not self._channel_read:
            self.peer_leases()
        if self.channel_root:
            return self.channel_root, None
        if self.channel_standing == "not_a_device":
            return REPO_ROOT, None
        return None, self.channel_error or "this device's channel store is unknown"

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ inbox
    def _inbox_dir(self):
        return os.path.join(self.dir, "inbox")

    def _inbox_notes_path(self):
        return os.path.join(self._inbox_dir(), "notes.jsonl")

    def _inbox_offset_path(self):
        return os.path.join(self._inbox_dir(), "offset.json")

    def _inbox_seen_path(self, session):
        return os.path.join(self._inbox_dir(), "seen", f"{_safe(session)}.json")

    @staticmethod
    def _normalized_note(line):
        if '"env:kind=note"' not in line:
            return None
        row = json.loads(line)
        tags = (row.get("record") or {}).get("classifiedAs") or []
        if "env:kind=note" not in tags:
            return None
        fields = {}
        via = None
        for tag in tags:
            if not isinstance(tag, str):
                continue
            if tag.startswith("env:") and "=" in tag:
                key, value = tag[4:].split("=", 1)
                fields[key] = value
            elif tag.startswith("via:did:key:"):
                via = tag[4:]
        if not row.get("cid") or not fields.get("session") or "text" not in fields:
            return None
        return {"cid": row["cid"], "at": float(fields["at"]), "from_device": via,
                "session": fields["session"], "to": fields.get("to") or None,
                "text": fields["text"]}

    @staticmethod
    def _read_json(path, default):
        try:
            with open(path) as f:
                return json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):
            return default

    def _scan_inbox(self):
        """Copy only new folded notes into the berth's small, stable stream. The source offset is
        device-wide; a shorter or different store is read again from zero, with CIDs keeping the
        normalized stream append-only so session cursors remain valid."""
        root = self.channel_root or self.cached_channel_root() or REPO_ROOT
        source = os.path.join(root, ".eprfs", "status", "flows.jsonl")
        size = os.stat(source).st_size
        state = self._read_json(self._inbox_offset_path(), {})
        offset = state.get("offset", 0) if state.get("source") == source else 0
        if not isinstance(offset, int) or offset < 0 or size < offset:
            offset = 0
        if size == offset:
            return

        os.makedirs(self._inbox_dir(), exist_ok=True)
        notes = []
        notes_path = self._inbox_notes_path()
        try:
            with open(notes_path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
                notes = [json.loads(line) for line in f if line.strip()]
        except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):
            notes = []
        known = {note.get("cid") for note in notes}
        added = []
        with open(source, "rb") as f:
            f.seek(offset)
            while True:
                raw = f.readline()
                if not raw or not raw.endswith(b"\n"):
                    break
                offset = f.tell()
                if b'"env:kind=note"' not in raw:
                    continue
                try:
                    note = self._normalized_note(raw.decode("utf-8"))
                except (UnicodeDecodeError, ValueError, TypeError):
                    continue
                if note and note["cid"] not in known:
                    known.add(note["cid"])
                    added.append(note)
        if added:
            tmp = f"{notes_path}.{os.getpid()}.tmp"
            with open(tmp, "w") as f:
                for note in notes + added:
                    f.write(json.dumps(note, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
            os.replace(tmp, notes_path)
        write_json_atomic(self._inbox_offset_path(), {"source": source, "offset": offset})

    def inbox(self, session, mark=True, include_seen=False):
        """Notes addressed to `session`, plus household notes since it moored. Fail-open: an inbox
        is an attention aid and must never impede the session or the channel writer."""
        try:
            with self._locked("inbox"):
                os.makedirs(os.path.join(self._inbox_dir(), "seen"), exist_ok=True)
                self._scan_inbox()
                seen_path = self._inbox_seen_path(session)
                seen = self._read_json(seen_path, {}).get("offset", 0)
                mooring = self._read_mooring(session)
                moored_at = mooring.get("moored_at") if mooring else None
                delivered = []
                end = 0 if include_seen else seen
                try:
                    with open(self._inbox_notes_path(), encoding="utf-8") as f:
                        if not include_seen:
                            f.seek(seen)
                        while True:
                            line = f.readline()
                            if not line:
                                break
                            end = f.tell()
                            note = json.loads(line)
                            if note.get("session") == session:
                                continue
                            addressed = note.get("to") == session
                            household = (not note.get("to") and moored_at is not None
                                         and note.get("at", 0) >= moored_at)
                            if addressed or household:
                                delivered.append(note)
                except FileNotFoundError:
                    pass
                if mark:
                    write_json_atomic(seen_path, {"offset": end})
                return delivered
        except Exception:
            return []

    @staticmethod
    def _note_line(note, session, now):
        device = note.get("from_device")
        short = (device.split(":")[-1][:10] + "…") if device else "this device"
        sender = str(note.get("session") or "?")
        text = " ".join(str(note.get("text") or "").split())
        if len(text) > 600:
            text = text[:599] + "…"
        direct = " to you" if note.get("to") == session else ""
        # Another device's words are data for the reader, never instructions to it.
        return (f"NOTE from {short}/{sender[:8]} {_age(now - note.get('at', now))} ago{direct} "
                f"(untrusted text from another device): «{text}»")

    @staticmethod
    def _reply_hint(session, notes):
        """A reply command only for a well-formed sender id: the id comes from the sender's record."""
        sender = str(notes[-1].get("session") or "")
        if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9-]{0,63}", sender):
            return None
        return f'reply: berth say --session {session} --to {sender} "…"'

    def inbox_lines(self, session):
        # Hook path: notes only. A ready-made command in an agent's context is an action surface.
        try:
            notes = self.inbox(session)
            if not notes:
                return ""
            return "\n".join(self._note_line(note, session, self.now()) for note in notes)
        except Exception:
            return ""

    def ledger(self, n=30):
        """The last n readable events. Per-line tolerant: a torn or NUL-padded line (a crash mid-append,
        a restart that zero-filled the tail) costs that line, never the whole record."""
        try:
            with open(self.ledger_path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
                lines = f.readlines()
        except OSError:
            return []
        out = []
        for line in lines:
            line = line.lstrip("\x00").strip()
            if not line:
                continue
            try:
                ev = json.loads(line)
            except json.JSONDecodeError:
                continue
            if isinstance(ev, dict):
                out.append(ev)
        return out[-n:] if n else out

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ observation
    def observation(self):
        """The `_observation` emitter module, or None — fail-open: a missing emitter costs the pain
        record, never the claim."""
        if self._obs is None:
            try:
                if HOOKS_DIR not in sys.path:
                    sys.path.insert(0, HOOKS_DIR)
                import _observation  # noqa: E402
                self._obs = _observation
            except Exception:
                self._obs = False
        return self._obs or None

    def _emit_pain(self, value, reason, **env):
        obs = self.observation()
        if obs is None or self._fold_refused_under_test(REPO_ROOT):
            return False
        try:
            if not obs.available():
                return False
            return bool(obs.emit(OVERRUN_MEASURE, ".", int(round(value)), reason=reason,
                                 env={k: v for k, v in env.items() if v is not None}, root=REPO_ROOT))
        except Exception:
            return False

    def _marker(self, lease):
        return os.path.join(self.emitted_dir, f"{_safe(lease.get('holder'))}-{lease.get('claimed_at')}")

    def _write_marker(self, lease):
        try:
            os.makedirs(self.emitted_dir, exist_ok=True)
            with open(self._marker(lease), "w") as f:
                f.write(str(round(self.now(), 3)))
        except OSError:
            pass

    def hold_summary(self, days=7):
        """Completed holds, by resource/session, released in the window. Renewals do not
        restart the hold. Unreleased/reaped claims have no measured end and are excluded.
        Refusals belong to the requesting session, not to the incumbent they name.
        """
        now = self.now()
        start = now - days * 86400
        pending, groups = {}, {}

        def group(key):
            return groups.setdefault(key, {"durations": [], "refusals": 0})

        for ev in self.ledger(0):
            at = ev.get("at")
            resource, session = ev.get("resource"), ev.get("session")
            if not isinstance(at, (int, float)) or not isinstance(resource, str) or not isinstance(session, str):
                continue
            if at > now:
                continue
            key = (resource, session)
            kind = ev.get("kind")
            if kind == "claim":
                pending[key] = at
                prior = ev.get("took_over_from")
                if prior:
                    pending.pop((resource, prior), None)
            elif kind == "release":
                holders = [session] + (ev.get("forced_from") or "").split(",")
                for holder in set(holders):
                    held = (resource, holder)
                    since = pending.pop(held, None)
                    if since is not None and start <= at and at >= since:
                        group(held)["durations"].append(at - since)
            elif kind == "reap":
                pending.pop(key, None)
            elif kind == "refuse" and at >= start:
                group(key)["refusals"] += 1
        return groups

    def reap(self):
        """Prune under the same lock as touch/claim. A stale heartbeat alone never kills
        a living process's mooring. Reaping is not a release-time measurement.
        """
        removed = {"moorings": [], "leases": []}
        with self._locked():
            now = self.now()
            for session, m in self.moorings().items():
                if now - m.get("last_seen", 0) < m.get("ttl_s", self.mooring_ttl_s):
                    continue
                pid = m.get("pid")
                if pid and self.pid_alive(pid):
                    want, have = m.get("pid_start"), self.pid_start(pid)
                    if want is None or have is None or want == have:
                        continue
                os.remove(self._moor_path(session))
                removed["moorings"].append(session)
                self.record("unmoor", session=session, reason="reap")
            leases = self.leases()
            for key, value in list(leases.items()):
                slots = isinstance(value, list)
                kept = []
                for lease in value if slots else [value]:
                    ttl = lease.get("ttl_s")
                    expired = ttl is not None and now >= lease.get("since", 0) + ttl
                    if expired or not self.holder_is_live(lease):
                        resource = key.removesuffix("/slots")
                        session = lease.get("holder")
                        removed["leases"].append({"resource": resource, "holder": session})
                        self.record("reap", resource=resource, session=session, reason="expired",
                                    expired_at=lease.get("since", 0) + ttl if ttl is not None else None)
                    else:
                        kept.append(lease)
                if kept:
                    leases[key] = kept if slots else kept[0]
                else:
                    del leases[key]
            if removed["leases"]:
                self._write_leases(leases)
        return removed

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ moorings
    def moorings(self):
        out = {}
        for name in os.listdir(self.moor_dir):
            if not name.endswith(".json"):
                continue
            try:
                with open(os.path.join(self.moor_dir, name)) as f:
                    m = json.load(f)
                out[m["session"]] = m
            except Exception:
                continue
        return out

    def mooring(self, session):
        return self.moorings().get(session)

    def is_live(self, m):
        """A mooring is live while its heartbeat is inside its ttl AND, when it carries a runtime-
        asserted pid, that process is alive in the SAME incarnation (start time) it moored with."""
        if not m:
            return False
        pid = m.get("pid")
        if pid:
            if not self.pid_alive(pid):
                return False
            want = m.get("pid_start")
            if want is not None:
                have = self.pid_start(pid)
                if have is not None and have != want:
                    return False  # the pid was reused by another process
        return (self.now() - m.get("last_seen", 0)) < m.get("ttl_s", self.mooring_ttl_s)

    def _read_mooring(self, session):
        try:
            with open(self._moor_path(session)) as f:
                return json.load(f)
        except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):
            return None

    def _assert_pid(self, m, pid):
        if pid:
            m["pid"] = int(pid)
            start = self.pid_start(pid)
            if start is not None:
                m["pid_start"] = start
            else:
                m.pop("pid_start", None)

    def moor(self, session, **fields):
        with envelope_guard(session, self.dir), self._locked():
            return self._moor_locked(session, **fields)

    def _moor_locked(self, session, **fields):
        m = self._read_mooring(session) or {"session": session, "moored_at": round(self.now(), 3)}
        pid = fields.pop("pid", None)
        for k, v in fields.items():
            if v is not None:
                m[k] = v
        self._assert_pid(m, pid)
        m.setdefault("recipient", {})
        for k in ("model", "lab", "runtime"):
            if m.get(k):
                m["recipient"][k] = m[k]
        m["recipient"]["session"] = session
        m.setdefault("bounds", {})
        if m.get("writes"):
            m["bounds"]["write_set"] = m["writes"]
        m["bounds"]["ttl_s"] = m.get("ttl_s", self.mooring_ttl_s)
        m.setdefault("ttl_s", self.mooring_ttl_s)
        m["last_seen"] = round(self.now(), 3)
        write_json_atomic(self._moor_path(session), m)
        self.record("moor", session=session, recipient=m["recipient"], provider=m.get("principal"),
                    task=m.get("task"), bounds=m["bounds"], reads="nacks/1")
        return m

    def touch(self, session, pid=None):
        """Heartbeat (and, from a hook, re-assert the runtime pid + incarnation). Serialized with every
        other mooring/lease writer and published atomically, so a concurrent claimant never reads a
        half-written mooring as a dead holder."""
        with envelope_guard(session, self.dir), self._locked():
            m = self._read_mooring(session)
            if not m:
                return None
            m["last_seen"] = round(self.now(), 3)
            self._assert_pid(m, pid)
            write_json_atomic(self._moor_path(session), m)
            return m

    def unmoor(self, session):
        with envelope_guard(session, self.dir):
            return self._unmoor(session)

    def _unmoor(self, session):
        """Cleanup under a caller-held lifecycle guard (including native close/GC)."""
        for res in {key.removesuffix("/slots") for key in self.leases()}:
            self._release(res, session, reason="unmoor")
        with self._locked():
            try:
                os.remove(self._moor_path(session))
            except FileNotFoundError:
                return
            self.record("unmoor", session=session)

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ leases
    def leases(self):
        try:
            with open(self.leases_path) as f:
                return json.load(f)
        except Exception:
            return {}

    def _write_leases(self, leases):
        write_json_atomic(self.leases_path, leases)

    def holder_is_live(self, lease):
        if not lease:
            return False
        ttl = lease.get("ttl_s")
        if ttl is not None and (self.now() - lease.get("since", 0)) > ttl:
            return False
        return self.is_live(self.mooring(lease.get("holder")))

    def live_leases(self, leases, resource):
        """Both storage shapes count, even after the declared capacity changes."""
        candidates = [leases.get(resource)] + leases.get(resource + "/slots", [])
        return [lease for lease in candidates if self.holder_is_live(lease)]

    def raw_lease(self, resource):
        """The single-slot lease record as stored, live or not (status renders an expired one)."""
        lease = self.leases().get(resource)
        return lease if isinstance(lease, dict) else None

    def class_spec(self, resource, klass):
        """The policy row for `klass` on `resource`, or None when the resource declares no classes."""
        table = self.classes.get(resource)
        if not table:
            return None
        if klass not in table:
            raise BerthUsage(f"{resource} has no lease class {klass!r} "
                             f"(pool-policy.json berth.classes.{resource}: {'|'.join(sorted(table))})")
        spec = table[klass]
        return spec if isinstance(spec, dict) else {}

    def _expired_after(self, cur):
        """Seconds the lapsed lease `cur` was held before it expired (ttl) or was abandoned (mooring)."""
        start = cur.get("claimed_at", cur.get("since"))
        if start is None:
            return None
        now = self.now()
        ttl = cur.get("ttl_s")
        end = cur.get("since", start) + ttl if ttl is not None else now
        return round(max(0, min(end, now) - start))

    def _renew(self, lease, ttl_s, note, seat, klass=None, session_source=None, closure=None):
        """Reset `since` (never `claimed_at`). Without an explicit ttl the hold stops at the class's
        max_ttl_s counted from claimed_at; an explicit ttl is itself capped. Returns a refusal
        reason, or None when renewed."""
        now = round(self.now(), 3)
        claimed = lease.get("claimed_at", lease.get("since", now))
        lease_class = klass or lease.get("class")
        spec = (self.classes.get(lease.get("resource")) or {}).get(lease_class) if lease_class else None
        cap = int(spec["max_ttl_s"]) if isinstance(spec, dict) and spec.get("max_ttl_s") else None
        if ttl_s is not None:
            ttl = min(int(ttl_s), cap) if cap else int(ttl_s)
        else:
            ttl = lease.get("ttl_s")
            if cap:
                remaining = int(claimed + cap - now)
                if remaining <= 0:
                    self.record("refuse", resource=lease.get("resource"), session=lease.get("holder"),
                                reason="max_ttl", max_ttl_s=cap, claimed_at=claimed, **{"class": lease_class})
                    return (f"the {lease_class} hold reached its {cap}s cap (claimed {_age(now - claimed)} ago) — "
                            f"release it, or renew with an explicit --ttl (capped at {cap}s)")
                ttl = min(ttl, remaining) if ttl is not None else remaining
        lease["since"] = now
        lease["claimed_at"] = claimed
        lease["ttl_s"] = ttl
        lease["note"] = note or lease.get("note")
        if lease_class:
            lease["class"] = lease_class
        if seat:
            lease["seat"] = seat
        if closure is not None:
            lease["closure"] = closure
        self.record("renew", resource=lease.get("resource"), session=lease.get("holder"), ttl_s=ttl,
                    claimed_at=claimed, seat=seat, note=note, session_source=session_source,
                    closure=lease.get("closure"), **_lease_times(lease), **{"class": lease_class})
        return None

    def _new_lease(self, resource, session, note, ttl_s, klass, seat, closure=None):
        now = round(self.now(), 3)
        lease = {"resource": resource, "holder": session, "since": now, "claimed_at": now,
                 "note": note, "ttl_s": ttl_s, "class": klass, "action": "use"}
        if seat:
            lease["seat"] = seat
        if closure is not None:
            lease["closure"] = closure
        return lease

    def claim_preflight(self, resource, ttl_s=None, klass=None, override=False):
        """Pure refusals precede session resolution and all lifecycle locking."""
        klass = klass or DEFAULT_CLASS
        if self.policy_error:
            return (f"pool-policy {self.policy_error} — no claim is taken while the policy cannot "
                                 f"say which resources are shared")
        explicit_ttl = ttl_s is not None
        if explicit_ttl:
            ttl_s = int(ttl_s)
            if ttl_s <= 0:
                raise BerthUsage("--ttl must be a positive number of seconds")
        spec = self.class_spec(resource, klass)
        if spec is not None:
            if spec.get("allowed") is False:
                alt = spec.get("alternative") or "a measurement peer"
                if not override:
                    return (f"{klass}-class work does not run on the dev berth — author it with "
                                         f"`{alt}` (rung H: --on jessica; rung A: --on adam)")
                if not explicit_ttl:
                    raise BerthUsage(f"a declared override declares its hold: MEASURE_ON_DEV_BERTH=1 berth claim "
                                     f"{resource} --class {klass} --ttl SECONDS --note '<why>'")
            if spec.get("daemon"):
                # The daemon lease is the household being UP, not a bounded run: no ttl, never taken
                # over by expiry — only when its holder's mooring is dead.
                if explicit_ttl:
                    raise BerthUsage(f"the {klass} class on {resource} is a daemon lease and takes no --ttl "
                                     f"(a bounded run claims verify)")
                ttl_s = None
            elif not explicit_ttl and spec.get("default_ttl_s"):
                ttl_s = int(spec["default_ttl_s"])
            cap = spec.get("max_ttl_s")
            if cap and explicit_ttl and ttl_s > int(cap):
                return (f"a {klass} lease on {resource} holds at most {int(cap)}s and --ttl {ttl_s} is "
                                     f"longer — declare it measure (`just measure <scope>`, or "
                                     f"MEASURE_ON_DEV_BERTH=1 --class measure --ttl {ttl_s})")
        return None

    def claim(self, resource, session, note=None, ttl_s=None, klass=None, seat=None, override=False,
              session_source=None, offline_ok=False, closure=None):
        """Returns (ok, lease, reason). A live holder that is not us ⇒ refused (exit 3): the honest
        answer is 'held by X since T', never a silent queue. Capacity > 1 is modelled as slots.

        The class table routes: a class the policy marks `allowed: false` is refused with its named
        alternative unless `override` (MEASURE_ON_DEV_BERTH=1) declares the hold — then it claims,
        writes a `kind: override` row and emits dev-berth-held-by-measure@1 = ttl immediately.
        A steward-scoped resource is then settled across this person's devices (`_settle_steward`);
        `offline_ok` records a delayed override of an `unconfirmed` one.
        A steward record that cannot reach the device's channel store refuses a claim, and leaves a
        renew held but returns ok=None: kept here, not confirmed to the other devices.
        Raises BerthUsage for a mis-stated claim (unknown class, override without --ttl)."""
        reason = self.claim_preflight(resource, ttl_s, klass, override)
        if reason:
            return False, None, reason
        with envelope_guard(session, self.dir):
            return self._claim_live(resource, session, note, ttl_s, klass, seat, override,
                                    session_source, offline_ok, closure)

    def _claim_live(self, resource, session, note, ttl_s, klass, seat, override,
                    session_source, offline_ok, closure=None):
        klass = klass or DEFAULT_CLASS
        explicit_ttl = ttl_s is not None
        if explicit_ttl:
            ttl_s = int(ttl_s)
        spec = self.class_spec(resource, klass) or {}
        overriding = spec.get("allowed") is False and override
        if spec.get("daemon"):
            ttl_s = None
        elif not explicit_ttl and spec.get("default_ttl_s"):
            ttl_s = int(spec["default_ttl_s"])
        steward = self.steward_scoped(resource)
        seen = None
        renewing = False
        if steward:
            steward, seen, renewing, refused = self._steward_precheck(resource, session, klass)
            if refused:
                return False, None, refused
            if renewing == "unreadable":
                # Preserve a held lease when the view itself is unavailable. The renew is still
                # recorded, and the fold failure below says it was not confirmed elsewhere.
                steward = False
        with self._locked():
            ok, lease, reason = self._claim_locked(resource, session, note, ttl_s if explicit_ttl else None,
                                                   ttl_s, klass, seat, overriding, session_source,
                                                   seen=seen, closure=closure)
        failed = self.take_fold_failures(resource) if ok else []
        if failed:
            if renewing or reason.startswith("renewed"):
                # The lease stays: it was held before. Its renew did not cross, so say so.
                return None, lease, (f"renewed here, but {failed[0]} — the other devices still hold its "
                                     f"earlier terms")
            self._release(resource, session, reason=f"steward: {failed[0]}")
            self.take_fold_failures(resource)
            return False, None, failed[0]
        if ok and steward:
            return self._settle_steward(resource, session, lease, offline_ok, renewal=bool(renewing))
        if ok and overriding:
            self.record("override", resource=resource, session=session, holder=session, ttl_s=ttl_s,
                        claimed_at=lease.get("claimed_at"), reason=note, seat=seat,
                        session_source=session_source, **{"class": klass})
            # Every declared override is pain on the record the moment the hold starts. Its marker
            # stops the overrun check from counting the same lease a second time.
            with self._locked("emit"):
                landed = self._emit_pain(
                    ttl_s or 0, f"declared override: {resource} held by {session} as {klass} for {ttl_s}s on "
                    f"the dev berth — {note or 'no reason given'}", resource=resource, kind="override",
                    **{"class": klass})
                if landed and lease.get("ttl_s"):
                    self._write_marker(lease)
            reason += (f"; declared override — {OVERRUN_MEASURE} = {ttl_s}s "
                       + ("emitted" if landed else "NOT emitted (no `epr` emitter); the override row is the record"))
        return ok, lease, reason

    def _claim_locked(self, resource, session, note, explicit_ttl, ttl_s, klass, seat, overriding, session_source=None,
                      seen=None, closure=None):
        if resource not in self.capacities:
            self.capacities[resource] = 1
        leases = self.leases()
        cap = self.capacities[resource]
        live = self.live_leases(leases, resource)
        mine = [lease for lease in live if lease.get("holder") == session]
        if mine:
            covered = None
            for lease in mine:
                held_class = lease.get("class")
                if held_class and held_class != klass:
                    held_spec = (self.classes.get(resource) or {}).get(held_class)
                    if isinstance(held_spec, dict) and held_spec.get("daemon"):
                        # A lane under the holder's OWN daemon lease: covered, the daemon lease is
                        # unchanged (the lane is fenced by its own deadline, not by this lease).
                        covered = held_class
                        self.record("renew", resource=resource, session=session, covered_by=held_class,
                                    requested_class=klass, ttl_s=ttl_s, claimed_at=lease.get("claimed_at"),
                                    seat=seat, note=note, session_source=session_source,
                                    closure=closure if closure is not None else lease.get("closure"),
                                    **_lease_times(lease))
                        continue
                    self.record("refuse", resource=resource, session=session, reason="class-transition",
                                held_class=held_class, session_source=session_source, **{"class": klass})
                    return False, lease, (f"you hold {resource} as {held_class}; a {klass} claim is a class "
                                          f"transition — release it first (`berth release {resource}`), "
                                          f"then claim {klass}")
                refused = self._renew(lease, explicit_ttl, note, seat, klass=None if held_class else klass,
                                      session_source=session_source, closure=closure)
                if refused:
                    return False, lease, refused
            self._write_leases(leases)
            return True, mine[0], (f"renewed — covered by your {covered} daemon lease" if covered else "renewed")
        if len(live) >= cap:
            if cap == 1:
                # One slot: the refusal names THE holder as a record (who/claim callers index it).
                cur = live[0]
                self.record("refuse", resource=resource, session=session, holder=cur["holder"], since=cur.get("since"),
                            reason="held", **{"class": klass})
                return False, cur, f"held by {cur['holder']} since {time.strftime('%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime(cur['since']))}"
            holders = ",".join(lease["holder"] for lease in live)
            self.record("refuse", resource=resource, session=session, holder=holders, reason="held", **{"class": klass})
            return False, live, f"all {cap} slots held by {holders}"
        if cap == 1:
            cur = leases.get(resource)
            if cur and self.holder_is_live(cur):
                self.record("refuse", resource=resource, session=session, holder=cur["holder"], since=cur["since"],
                            reason="held", **{"class": klass})
                return False, cur, f"held by {cur['holder']} since {time.strftime('%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime(cur['since']))}"
            prior = cur["holder"] if cur else None
            takeover = prior if prior and prior != session else None
            lease = self._new_lease(resource, session, note, ttl_s, klass, seat, closure)
            leases[resource] = lease
            self._write_leases(leases)
            self.record("claim", resource=resource, session=session, note=note, ttl_s=ttl_s,
                        claimed_at=lease["claimed_at"], seat=seat, took_over_from=takeover,
                        session_source=session_source, seen=seen, closure=closure, **_lease_times(lease),
                        expired_after_s=self._expired_after(cur) if cur else None, **{"class": klass})
            if takeover:
                return True, lease, "taken over from a stale holder"
            return True, lease, "re-claimed after its own lease lapsed" if prior else "claimed"
        slots = [l for l in leases.get(resource + "/slots", []) if self.holder_is_live(l)]
        lease = self._new_lease(resource, session, note, ttl_s, klass, seat, closure)
        slots.append(lease)
        leases[resource + "/slots"] = slots
        self._write_leases(leases)
        self.record("claim", resource=resource, session=session, note=note, ttl_s=ttl_s,
                    claimed_at=lease["claimed_at"], seat=seat, session_source=session_source, seen=seen,
                    closure=closure, **_lease_times(lease), **{"class": klass})
        return True, lease, "claimed"

    def release(self, resource, session, reason=None, force=False):
        """Give back this session's lease. `force` gives back WHOEVER holds it (a forced `mesh stop`
        took the household down under them) and says so on the record."""
        with envelope_guard(session, self.dir):
            return self._release(resource, session, reason, force)

    def _release(self, resource, session, reason=None, force=False):
        """Release under the lifecycle guard held by claim, unmoor or release."""
        with self._locked():
            leases = self.leases()
            changed = []
            cur = leases.get(resource)
            if cur and (force or cur.get("holder") == session):
                del leases[resource]
                changed.append(cur.get("holder"))
            slots = leases.get(resource + "/slots")
            if slots:
                kept = [l for l in slots if not force and l.get("holder") != session]
                if len(kept) != len(slots):
                    changed += [l.get("holder") for l in slots if l not in kept]
                    leases[resource + "/slots"] = kept
            if changed:
                self._write_leases(leases)
                forced = [h for h in changed if h != session]
                self.record("release", resource=resource, session=session, reason=reason,
                            forced_from=",".join(map(str, forced)) if forced else None)
        return bool(changed)

    def owner_check(self, resource, session, action, force=False, note=None):
        """May `session` do `action` (a destructive act on the resource, e.g. stop the household)?
        Refused while another LIVE session holds the resource; `force` proceeds and writes an
        `override` row naming whom it overrode. A steward-scoped resource also reads the steward lease
        view: another device's lease refuses, `force` or not, and so does a view that cannot be read.
        Returns (ok, holders, reason)."""
        if self.policy_error:
            return False, [], f"pool-policy {self.policy_error}"
        if self.steward_scoped(resource):
            view, err = self.peer_leases()
            if err:
                return False, [], err
            standing = view.get("standing")
            if standing == "not_a_device":
                print(self._not_a_device_line(resource, "checking"), file=sys.stderr)
            elif standing == "revoked":
                return False, [], f"revoked: {view.get('why')}"
            elif standing != "device":
                return False, [], f"the steward lease view names no standing (`{standing}`)"
            else:
                verdict = view.get(resource) or {}
                if verdict.get("verdict") == "held_by":
                    self.record("refuse", resource=resource, session=session, reason="owner", action=action,
                                holder=f"{verdict['device']}/{verdict['session']}")
                    return False, [verdict], steward_reason(verdict, self._view_now(view))
                if verdict.get("verdict") == "unconfirmed":
                    mine = self._mine(resource, session)
                    fence_after_s = None
                    if verdict.get("fenced") and mine and mine.get("ttl_s") is not None:
                        fence_after_s = max(0, int(mine["ttl_s"]) - self.fence_margin_s)
                    return False, [verdict], steward_reason(
                        verdict, self._view_now(view), fence_after_s)
        with self._locked():
            live = self.live_leases(self.leases(), resource)
            others = [l for l in live if l.get("holder") != session]
            if not others:
                return True, [], "yours" if live else "free"
            holders = ",".join(f"{l['holder']} ({l.get('class') or '?'}, {_age(self.now() - l.get('claimed_at', l['since']))})"
                               for l in others)
            if force:
                self.record("override", resource=resource, session=session, action=action,
                            holder=",".join(l["holder"] for l in others), reason=note)
                return True, others, f"forced over {holders}"
            self.record("refuse", resource=resource, session=session, reason="owner", action=action,
                        holder=",".join(l["holder"] for l in others))
            return False, others, f"{action} refused — {resource} is held by {holders}"

    def overrun_check(self, resource="mesh"):
        """Emit dev-berth-held-by-measure@1 (value = seconds held since claimed_at) ONCE for a lease
        held past its ttl, marked under emitted/<holder>-<claimed_at>. Returns the seconds emitted, or
        None. No marker without a landed emit, so an unavailable emitter retries on a later call."""
        lease = self.raw_lease(resource)
        if not lease or lease.get("claimed_at") is None or not lease.get("ttl_s"):
            return None
        if self.now() - lease["claimed_at"] <= lease["ttl_s"]:
            return None
        # check → emit → mark is one critical section: two prompt-triggered checks cannot both emit.
        with self._locked("emit"):
            lease = self.raw_lease(resource)
            if not lease or lease.get("claimed_at") is None or not lease.get("ttl_s"):
                return None
            claimed, ttl = lease["claimed_at"], lease["ttl_s"]
            held = self.now() - claimed
            if held <= ttl or os.path.exists(self._marker(lease)):
                return None
            klass = lease.get("class")
            if not self._emit_pain(held, f"{resource} lease held by {lease.get('holder')} as {klass} for "
                                   f"{_age(held)} past a {_age(ttl)} ttl (claimed_at {claimed})",
                                   resource=resource, kind="overrun", **{"class": klass}):
                return None
            self._write_marker(lease)
        self.record("overrun", resource=resource, holder=lease.get("holder"), ttl_s=ttl, claimed_at=claimed,
                    held_s=round(held), measure=OVERRUN_MEASURE, **{"class": klass})
        return round(held)

    def who(self, resource):
        leases = self.leases()
        live = self.live_leases(leases, resource)
        if len(live) == 1 and live[0] is leases.get(resource):
            return {**live[0], **_lease_times(live[0])}
        return [{**lease, **_lease_times(lease)} for lease in live] or None

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ steward-scoped resources
    def steward_scoped(self, resource):
        """Shared by every device of this person (pool-policy `scope: steward`), not this workspace's
        own: named, or under a declared prefix (`lane:` covers `lane:<id>`, never bare `lane:`)."""
        return resource in self.steward_names or any(
            resource.startswith(p) and len(resource) > len(p) for p in self.steward_prefixes)

    def epr_bin(self):
        """The `epr` a steward claim asks, found the way `just status device` finds it ($EPR_BIN,
        PATH through the native bin store), or None when there is no executable one."""
        path = self.epr or os.environ.get("EPR_BIN")
        if path is None:
            sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(REPO_ROOT, ".claude", "scripts"))
            from _lib import epr_client
            path = epr_client.resolve_binary(dict(os.environ))
        return path if path and os.path.isfile(path) and os.access(path, os.X_OK) else None

    @staticmethod
    def device_key_path():
        """Where this workspace's device key is, as `just status device` reads it."""
        # Key presence remains observable when no evaluator exists. This is only the documented
        # path convention; reading/validating device identity belongs to native epr.
        return os.environ.get("ELOHIM_DEVICE_KEY_FILE") or os.path.join(
            os.environ.get("XDG_CONFIG_HOME") or os.path.expanduser("~/.config"),
            "elohim", "device", "ed25519.seed")

    def _no_epr(self):
        where = self.epr or "EPR_BIN or the native launcher on PATH"
        return (f"no `epr` binary to read the steward lease view (looked at {where}) — arrive it: "
                f"`epr device arrive` (or export EPR_BIN=<path>); this workspace is a device (it has a "
                f"device key), and a steward-scoped claim is never taken unconfirmed")

    @staticmethod
    def _not_a_device_line(resource, doing="claiming"):
        return (f"berth: {resource} is steward-scoped but this workspace is not one of its steward's devices "
                f"(run: just status device); {doing} locally only")

    def peer_leases(self, timeout=PEER_TIMEOUT_S):
        """(view, error): `epr peer leases --json` — this device's standing, its channel store and the
        steward lease view. An error whenever the view could not be computed: an unreadable view is
        never a free resource. Remembers the channel store, where steward records are written."""
        self._channel_read = True
        view, err = self._read_peer_leases(timeout)
        self.channel_error = err
        self.channel_standing = view.get("standing") if view else None
        store = view.get("store") if view and view.get("standing") == "device" else None
        self.channel_root = store if isinstance(store, str) and store else None
        if self.channel_root:
            self._remember_channel(self.channel_root)
        elif self.channel_standing in ("not_a_device", "revoked"):
            self._remember_channel(None)
        return view, err

    def _run_peer_leases(self, epr, timeout):
        try:
            return subprocess.run([epr, "peer", "leases", "--json", "--root", main_checkout(REPO_ROOT),
                                   "--policy", self.policy_path],
                                  capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=max(0.1, timeout)), None
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
            return None, f"the steward lease view did not answer: {e}"

    @staticmethod
    def _is_stale_epr(r):
        first = (r.stderr.strip().splitlines() or [""])[0].strip()
        return "unknown command" in first or first.startswith("usage:")

    def _read_peer_leases(self, timeout):
        epr = self.epr_bin()
        if not epr:
            # Without `epr`, the one fact berth can read is the device key: a workspace with none is
            # not a device (container scope); one with a key needs `epr` to say how it stands.
            key = self.device_key_path()
            if not os.path.isfile(key):
                return {"now": round(self.now() * 1000), "standing": "not_a_device", "device": None,
                        "store": None, "why": f"this workspace has no device key ({key})"}, None
            return None, self._no_epr()
        r, err = self._run_peer_leases(epr, timeout)
        if err:
            return None, err
        if r.returncode != 0:
            # The first line names what went wrong; later lines are usage or context.
            why = (r.stderr.strip().splitlines() or [f"exit {r.returncode}"])[0].strip()
            if self._is_stale_epr(r):
                why = f"{why} \u2014 {STALE_EPR_HINT.format(path=epr)}"
            return None, f"the steward lease view could not be computed: {why}"
        try:
            view = json.loads(r.stdout)
        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
            return None, f"the steward lease view is not JSON: {e}"
        if not isinstance(view, dict):
            return None, "the steward lease view is not an object"
        return view, None

    def _view_now(self, view):
        now = view.get("now")
        return now if isinstance(now, (int, float)) else round(self.now() * 1000)

    def _mine(self, resource, session):
        return next((lease for lease in self.live_leases(self.leases(), resource)
                     if lease.get("holder") == session), None)

    def _steward_precheck(self, resource, session, klass):
        """Before any steward lease is written: (steward, seen, renewing, refusal). A lease this session
        already holds is still read and settled after its renew; an unreadable view preserves the old
        effective lease but reports that its renew was not confirmed. A workspace that is not a device
        claims container-scoped, with one line; a revoked device or another device's lease already in
        the view refuses, and nothing is written. `seen` is what this device had folded, carried by the
        claim it writes."""
        mine = self._mine(resource, session)
        view, err = self.peer_leases()
        if err:
            if mine and mine.get("effective"):
                return True, None, "unreadable", None
            if not self.epr_bin():
                self.record("refuse", resource=resource, session=session, reason="no-epr", **{"class": klass})
            return True, None, False, err
        standing = view.get("standing")
        if standing == "not_a_device":
            print(self._not_a_device_line(resource), file=sys.stderr)
            return False, None, False, None
        if standing == "revoked":
            reason = f"revoked: {view.get('why')}"
            self.record("refuse", resource=resource, session=session, reason="revoked", **{"class": klass})
            return True, None, False, reason
        if standing != "device":
            return True, None, False, f"the steward lease view names no standing (`{standing}`)"
        verdict = view.get(resource)
        if isinstance(verdict, dict) and verdict.get("verdict") == "held_by":
            reason = steward_reason(verdict, self._view_now(view))
            self.record("refuse", resource=resource, session=session, reason="held",
                        holder=f"{verdict['device']}/{verdict['session']}", **{"class": klass})
            if mine:
                # This session's own unsettled lease lost: it must not linger here or on the channel.
                self._release(resource, session, reason=f"steward: {reason}")
            return True, None, False, reason
        seen = view.get("seen") if isinstance(view.get("seen"), dict) else {}
        return True, seen, "renewing" if mine else False, None

    def _mark_effective(self, resource, session, effective=True):
        with self._locked():
            leases = self.leases()
            for lease in [leases.get(resource)] + leases.get(resource + "/slots", []):
                if isinstance(lease, dict) and lease.get("holder") == session:
                    lease["effective"] = effective
            self._write_leases(leases)

    def _has_offline_override(self, resource, session, claimed_at):
        return any(row.get("kind") == "override" and row.get("resource") == resource
                   and row.get("session") == session and row.get("claimed_at") == claimed_at
                   and row.get("overrode") for row in self.ledger(0))

    def _settle_steward(self, resource, session, lease, offline_ok, renewal=False):
        """The lease is written (it crosses on this device's next head); read the view until it leaves
        pending, within confirm_wait_s (plus one second's grace; each read is given only the time left).
        Effective → claimed, and remembered as effective. held by → refused. unconfirmed → refused;
        offline_ok keeps it unconfirmed and writes the delayed override naming the silent device. A
        refusal releases the lease, so a claim that did not hold never blocks anyone — except that a
        renew is released only when another device's lease holds it, never on a view it could not read
        or confirm."""
        deadline = self.now() + self.confirm_wait_s + 1
        while True:
            view, err = self.peer_leases(timeout=min(PEER_TIMEOUT_S, deadline - self.now()))
            verdict = (view or {}).get(resource)
            kind = verdict.get("verdict") if isinstance(verdict, dict) else None
            left = deadline - self.now()
            if kind == "pending" and verdict.get("session") == session and left > 0:
                self.sleep(min(POLL_S, left))
                continue
            break
        held = False
        if err:
            reason = err
        elif kind is None:
            reason = (f"this device's lease on {resource} is not in its channel store (the dev-berth-events@1 fold "
                      f"did not land — is `epr flow note` working?), so no other device can see it")
        elif kind in ("held_by", "refused_by"):
            reason, held = steward_reason(verdict, self._view_now(view)), True
        elif verdict.get("session") != session:
            reason, held = f"held by {verdict.get('session')} on this device", True
        elif kind == "effective":
            self._mark_effective(resource, session)
            return True, lease, "renewed" if renewal else "claimed"
        elif kind == "unconfirmed":
            fence_after_s = None
            if verdict.get("fenced") and lease.get("ttl_s") is not None:
                fence_after_s = max(0, int(lease["ttl_s"]) - self.fence_margin_s)
                self._mark_effective(resource, session, False)
            reason = steward_reason(verdict, self._view_now(view), fence_after_s)
            if (offline_ok and not verdict.get("fenced")
                    and not self._has_offline_override(resource, session, lease.get("claimed_at"))):
                self.record("override", resource=resource, session=session, holder=session,
                            claimed_at=lease.get("claimed_at"), overrode=verdict.get("device"),
                            last_seen=verdict.get("last_seen"), reason=f"--offline-ok over {reason}",
                            **{"class": lease.get("class")})
                failed = self.take_fold_failures(resource)
                if failed:
                    self._release(resource, session, reason=f"steward: {failed[0]}")
                    return False, None, failed[0]
                delayed, delayed_err = self.peer_leases()
                delayed_verdict = (delayed or {}).get(resource)
                if delayed_err:
                    reason = f"override on the record, but {delayed_err}"
                elif isinstance(delayed_verdict, dict):
                    reason = steward_reason(delayed_verdict, self._view_now(delayed))
                return False, None, f"{reason} — override on the record"
        else:
            waiting = (verdict.get("waiting_on") or ["another device"])[0]
            reason = f"unconfirmed: {waiting} did not acknowledge within {self.confirm_wait_s}s"
        if held or not renewal:
            self._release(resource, session, reason=f"steward: {reason}")
        if kind in ("unconfirmed", "pending") and (view or {}).get("serving") is False:
            # Unacknowledged because this device never announced it: the cure is here.
            reason = f"{reason}\n{DAEMON_DOWN_LINE}"
        return False, None, reason

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ notes
    def say(self, session, text, to=None):
        return self.record("note", session=session, to=to, text=text)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- rendering

def _age(secs):
    secs = max(0, int(secs))
    return f"{secs}s" if secs < 90 else (f"{secs // 60}m" if secs < 5400 else f"{secs // 3600}h{(secs % 3600) // 60:02d}")


def _lease_times(lease):
    since, ttl = lease["since"], lease.get("ttl_s")
    return {"last_renewed_at": since, "expires_at": since + ttl if ttl is not None else None}


def _lease_description(lease, now):
    times = _lease_times(lease)
    expires = times["expires_at"]
    expiry = (f"expires in {_age(expires - now)} at {_rfc3339(expires * 1000)}"
              if expires is not None else "no expiry")
    terms = ", ".join(x for x in (lease.get("class"),
                                 f"ttl {_age(lease['ttl_s'])}" if lease.get("ttl_s") else None,
                                 f"last renewed {_age(now - times['last_renewed_at'])} ago", expiry) if x)
    return (f"held by {lease['holder']} for {_age(now - lease.get('claimed_at', lease['since']))} ({terms})"
            + (f" closure={lease['closure']}" if lease.get("closure") else "")
            + (f" — {lease['note']}" if lease.get("note") else ""))


def _guard_state(name):
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(CONFIG_DIR, name, "state.json")) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except Exception:
        return None


def render_status(b):
    now = b.now()
    lines = ["BERTH (this workspace as one blade — moorings · leases · capacity)"]
    ms = b.moorings()
    if not ms:
        lines.append("  moorings: none — `berth moor --session <id> --model <id> --lab <vendor> --task '<lane>'`")
    for s, m in sorted(ms.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1].get("last_seen", 0)):
        r = m.get("recipient", {})
        live = "live" if b.is_live(m) else "STALE"
        lines.append(f"  {live:5} {s:<14} {r.get('runtime', '?'):<12} {r.get('model', '?')}@{r.get('lab', '?')}"
                     f"  for {m.get('principal') or '?'}  task={m.get('task') or '-'}  seen {_age(now - m.get('last_seen', now))} ago")
    leases = b.leases()
    caps = b.capacities
    # Read the other devices once: a resource free here may be held on one of them, and the top
    # list is what a waiting reader matches, so it names that holder instead of saying "free".
    view, view_line = _steward_view(b)
    rules_line = _rules_line(view)
    if rules_line:
        lines.append(rules_line)
    now_ms = b._view_now(view) if view else round(now * 1000)
    elsewhere = {res: verdict for res, verdict in (view or {}).items()
                 if isinstance(verdict, dict) and verdict.get("verdict") == "held_by"}
    lines.append("  leases:")
    for res in sorted(set(caps) | {k.split('/')[0] for k in leases}):
        holder = b.who(res)
        if isinstance(holder, list):
            desc = ", ".join(_lease_description(lease, now) for lease in holder) or "free"
            lines.append(f"    {res:<11} {len(holder)}/{caps.get(res, 1)}  {desc}")
        elif holder:
            verdict = (view or {}).get(res)
            if (isinstance(verdict, dict) and verdict.get("verdict") == "unconfirmed"
                    and verdict.get("session") == holder.get("holder")):
                fence_after_s = None
                if verdict.get("fenced") and holder.get("ttl_s") is not None:
                    fence_after_s = max(0, int(holder["ttl_s"]) - b.fence_margin_s)
                lines.append(f"    {res:<11} {steward_reason(verdict, now_ms, fence_after_s)}")
            else:
                lines.append(f"    {res:<11} {_lease_description(holder, now)}")
        else:
            raw = b.raw_lease(res)
            if raw and raw.get("holder"):
                held = _age(now - raw.get("claimed_at", raw.get("since", now)))
                if raw.get("ttl_s"):
                    lines.append(f"    {res:<11} EXPIRED {raw['holder']} — held {held} of a {_age(raw['ttl_s'])} "
                                 f"{raw.get('class') or 'unclassed'} ttl (takeover on next claim)")
                else:
                    lines.append(f"    {res:<11} EXPIRED {raw['holder']} — held {held}, mooring stale "
                                 f"(takeover on next claim)")
            elif res in elsewhere:
                lines.append(f"    {res:<11} {steward_reason(elsewhere[res], now_ms)} (another device)")
            elif view_line and b.steward_scoped(res):
                lines.append(f"    {res:<11} not held here — other devices unknown")
            else:
                lines.append(f"    {res:<11} free")
    lines += _other_devices_lines(b, view, view_line)
    groups = b.hold_summary()
    resources = sorted({resource for resource, _ in groups} | {"dev-integration"})
    lines.append("  holds (last 7 days, completed; refusals by requester):")
    def hold_line(resource, holder, durations, refusals):
        values = sorted(durations)
        # Nearest rank, as in the gate-cost p90 fold.
        p50 = values[(len(values) + 1) // 2 - 1] if values else None
        p90 = values[(len(values) * 9 + 9) // 10 - 1] if values else None
        stats = "/".join(_age(v) if v is not None else "unknown" for v in
                         (p50, p90, max(values) if values else None))
        return f"    {resource}{holder} hold p50/p90/max {stats} (n={len(values)}), refusals {refusals}"
    for resource in resources:
        selected = [(holder, stats) for (res, holder), stats in groups.items() if res == resource]
        lines.append(hold_line(resource, "", [d for _, stats in selected for d in stats["durations"]],
                               sum(stats["refusals"] for _, stats in selected)))
        for holder, stats in sorted(selected):
            lines.append(hold_line(resource, f" / {holder}", stats["durations"], stats["refusals"]))
    ram = _guard_state("ram-guard")
    io = _guard_state("io-guard")
    if ram:
        lines.append(f"  ram-guard: {ram.get('level', '?')} {ram.get('pct', '?')}% committed")
    if io:
        lines.append(f"  io-guard:  {io.get('level', '?')} write={io.get('write_mb_s', '?')}MB/s ({io.get('window_s', '?')}s)"
                     f" psi_full10={io.get('psi_full_avg10', '?')}% mode={io.get('mode', '?')} paused={len(io.get('paused', []))}")
    return "\n".join(lines)


def _rules_line(view):
    """The daemon-loaded advisory rules line from `epr peer leases --json`, when available."""
    rules = view.get("rules") if isinstance(view, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(rules, dict):
        return None
    if rules.get("state") == "loaded" and rules.get("short"):
        return f"  rules: {rules['short']}"
    if rules.get("state") == "reloading":
        return f"  rules: reloading — {rules.get('reason') or 'policy changed'}"
    return None


def _steward_view(b):
    """(view, None) when this device's fold of its steward's other devices was read, else (None, the
    one status line that says why not). Only a berth whose policy declares steward-scoped resources
    asks; a view it cannot read says so, never "none"."""
    if not (b.steward_names or b.steward_prefixes):
        return None, None
    if b.policy_error:
        return None, f"  other devices: unknown — pool-policy {b.policy_error}"
    view, err = b.peer_leases()
    if err:
        return None, f"  other devices: unknown — {err}"
    standing = view.get("standing")
    if standing == "not_a_device":
        return None, (f"  other devices: none — this workspace is not one of its steward's devices "
                      f"({view.get('why')}; run: just status device)")
    if standing != "device":
        return None, f"  other devices: none — {standing}: {view.get('why')}"
    return view, None


def _other_devices_lines(b, view, view_line):
    """The other devices of this person, as this device has folded them (`epr peer leases --json`:
    `others` and the `held_by` verdicts, replayed in each device's own record order): each one's last
    head, its open moorings and its steward-scoped leases, lane claims among them."""
    if view is None:
        return [view_line] if view_line else []
    now_ms = b._view_now(view)
    others = view.get("others") if isinstance(view.get("others"), dict) else {}
    held = {}
    for res, verdict in view.items():
        if isinstance(verdict, dict) and verdict.get("verdict") == "held_by":
            held.setdefault(verdict.get("device"), []).append((res, verdict))
    lines = ["  other devices (read from this device's fold of their records):"]
    if not others and not held:
        lines.append("    none — no other device is admitted on this roster")
    for did in sorted(set(others) | set(held)):
        info = others.get(did) or {}
        seen = info.get("last_seen")
        if seen is None:
            head = "SILENT: no head folded yet"
        else:
            age = now_ms - seen
            head = f"head seq {info.get('seq')} folded {_peer_age(age)} ago"
            if age > b.freshness_s * 1000:
                head += f" — SILENT past {b.freshness_s}s"
        lines.append(f"    device {did}  {head}")
        for session, since in sorted((info.get("moorings") or {}).items()):
            # A folded mooring is that device's latest moor record. Touches do not cross, so a long
            # session can be alive past the ttl; the label says only what the record shows.
            age = now_ms - since
            if age > b.mooring_ttl_s * 1000:
                lines.append(f"      STALE {session} — no moor record within the {b.mooring_ttl_s}s mooring "
                             f"ttl (last {_peer_age(age)} ago)")
            else:
                lines.append(f"      moored {session} since {_rfc3339(since)}")
        for res, verdict in sorted(held.get(did, []), key=lambda item: item[0]):
            line = f"      {res}  {steward_reason(verdict, now_ms)}"
            if verdict.get("override"):
                line += " — an override of this device's silence (offline-ok)"
            lines.append(line)
    return lines


def _fmt_ledger(ev):
    t = time.strftime("%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(ev.get("at", 0)))
    k = ev.get("kind")
    if k == "note":
        return f"{t} {ev.get('session')}→{ev.get('to') or 'all'}: {ev.get('text')}"
    if k in ("claim", "release", "refuse", "renew", "override", "overrun"):
        extra = f" [{ev['class']}{', ttl ' + _age(ev['ttl_s']) if ev.get('ttl_s') else ''}]" if ev.get("class") else ""
        extra += f" (holder {ev.get('holder')})" if ev.get("holder") and k != "override" else ""
        extra += f" took over from {ev['took_over_from']}" if ev.get("took_over_from") else ""
        extra += f" after {_age(ev['expired_after_s'])} expired" if ev.get("expired_after_s") is not None else ""
        extra += f" refused: {ev['reason']}" if k == "refuse" and ev.get("reason") else ""
        extra += f" → {ev['alternative']}" if ev.get("alternative") else ""
        extra += f" held {_age(ev['held_s'])}" if ev.get("held_s") is not None else ""
        extra += f" seat={ev['seat']}" if ev.get("seat") else ""
        extra += f" — {ev['reason']}" if k == "override" and ev.get("reason") else ""
        extra += f" — {ev['note']}" if ev.get("note") else ""
        return f"{t} {k:<7} {ev.get('resource')} by {ev.get('session') or ev.get('holder')}{extra}"
    if k == "moor":
        r = ev.get("recipient", {})
        return f"{t} moor    {ev.get('session')} {r.get('runtime', '?')} {r.get('model', '?')}@{r.get('lab', '?')} task={ev.get('task') or '-'}"
    if k == "shed":
        return f"{t} shed    {ev.get('guard')} {ev.get('action')} {ev.get('target')} (level {ev.get('level')}, holder {ev.get('holder')})"
    return f"{t} {k} {json.dumps({kk: vv for kk, vv in ev.items() if kk not in ('at', 'kind')})}"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cli

def _opt(argv, name, default=None):
    if name in argv:
        i = argv.index(name)
        if i + 1 < len(argv):
            v = argv[i + 1]
            del argv[i:i + 2]
            return v
    return default


_STORE_ERRNOS = {errno.EACCES, errno.EPERM, errno.ENOENT, errno.EROFS}


def _store_unavailable(exc, store):
    """An OSError on the berth store itself (its dir, lock, ledger, leases or moorings) — not one
    raised anywhere else. The store is the host session's coordination organ, never a guest's."""
    if not isinstance(exc, OSError) or exc.errno not in _STORE_ERRNOS:
        return False
    names = [n for n in (getattr(exc, "filename", None), getattr(exc, "filename2", None)) if n]
    root = os.path.realpath(store)
    return any(os.path.realpath(str(n)) == root or os.path.realpath(str(n)).startswith(root + os.sep)
               for n in names)


def main(argv):
    """Exit 4 when this invocation cannot open its store — e.g. the stage runner's guest (UID 65534,
    BERTH_DIR stripped) meeting the host's root-owned berth.lock: the lane proceeds unleased and says
    so, rather than dying with a traceback the wrapper would propagate."""
    store = store_dir()
    try:
        return _main(argv)
    except OSError as e:
        if not _store_unavailable(e, store):
            raise
        name = errno.errorcode.get(e.errno, str(e.errno))
        print(f"berth: store unavailable ({name} {e.filename}) — lane proceeds unleased", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_NO_SESSION


def _main(argv):
    argv = list(argv[1:])
    if not argv:
        argv = ["status"]
    cmd = argv.pop(0)
    if cmd in ("-h", "--help", "help") or "-h" in argv or "--help" in argv:
        # A flag is never a resource: `berth claim --help` once took a lease named "--help".
        print(__doc__.split("Commands:")[1].split("Resources")[0])
        return 0
    b = Berth()
    session = _opt(argv, "--session")
    source = "flag" if session else None
    if cmd == "status":
        print(render_status(b))
        return 0
    if cmd == "ledger":
        n = int(_opt(argv, "-n", "30"))
        for ev in b.ledger(n):
            print(_fmt_ledger(ev))
        return 0
    if cmd == "reap":
        removed = b.reap()
        print(f"berth: reaped {len(removed['moorings'])} moorings, {len(removed['leases'])} leases")
        return 0
    if cmd == "overrun-check":
        # Hook-facing (ram-guard's prompt event): never fails the caller, prints only on an emit.
        try:
            held = b.overrun_check(argv[0] if argv else "mesh")
        except Exception:
            held = None
        if held:
            print(f"{argv[0] if argv else 'mesh'}: {OVERRUN_MEASURE} = {held}s emitted")
        return 0
    if cmd == "who":
        if not argv:
            print("usage: berth who RESOURCE", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        print(json.dumps(b.who(argv[0])))
        return 0
    def resolve():
        if session:
            return session, source, None
        identity = resolve_session_identity()
        if identity["session"]:
            return identity["session"], "envelope", None
        return None, None, "berth: no P1 session; open an envelope in a registered runtime"

    claim_args = None
    if cmd == "claim":
        # Parsed and class-checked BEFORE the session is resolved: a class this berth does not run
        # is refused (exit 3) whether or not the caller can name itself.
        usage = ("usage: berth claim RESOURCE --session S [--class verify|measure|mesh] [--ttl SECONDS] [--note TEXT] "
                 "[--closure KEY] [--offline-ok]")
        ttl = _opt(argv, "--ttl")
        note = _opt(argv, "--note")
        klass = _opt(argv, "--class") or DEFAULT_CLASS
        closure = _opt(argv, "--closure")
        if "--closure" in argv or (closure is not None and (not closure or closure.startswith("--"))):
            print(usage, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        offline_ok = "--offline-ok" in argv
        argv = [a for a in argv if a != "--offline-ok"]
        if not argv:
            print(usage, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        try:
            ttl_s = int(ttl) if ttl else None
        except ValueError:
            print(f"berth: --ttl {ttl!r} is not a number of seconds\n{usage}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        res = argv[0]
        override = os.environ.get("MEASURE_ON_DEV_BERTH") == "1"
        try:
            reason = b.claim_preflight(res, ttl_s, klass, override)
        except BerthUsage as e:
            print(f"berth: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if reason:
            print(f"{res}: REFUSED — {reason}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
        claim_args = (res, note, ttl_s, klass, override, offline_ok, closure)

    if cmd == "owner-check":
        if not argv:
            print("usage: berth owner-check RESOURCE [--action ACTION] [--force] [--note TEXT]", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        action = _opt(argv, "--action") or "act"
        note = _opt(argv, "--note")
        force = "--force" in argv
        who_am_i = resolve()[0]
        ok, _, reason = b.owner_check(argv[0], who_am_i, action, force=force, note=note)
        if ok:
            if force and reason.startswith("forced"):
                print(f"{argv[0]}: {action} — {reason} (override on the record)", file=sys.stderr)
            return 0
        if b.steward_scoped(argv[0]):
            print(f"{argv[0]}: REFUSED — {reason}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
        print(f"{argv[0]}: REFUSED — {reason}. Ask them (`berth say --to <holder> …`), or override on the "
              f"record (MESH_STOP_FORCE=1 for `just mesh stop`)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3

    session, source, err = resolve()
    if not session:
        print(err, file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_NO_SESSION
    if cmd == "session-show":
        with b._locked():
            leases = {k: ([v for v in value if v.get("holder") == session] if isinstance(value, list)
                           else value) for k, value in b.leases().items()
                      if (any(v.get("holder") == session for v in value) if isinstance(value, list)
                          else value.get("holder") == session)}
            print(json.dumps({"mooring": b.mooring(session), "leases": leases}))
        return 0
    if cmd == "inbox":
        peek = "--peek" in argv
        include_seen = "--all" in argv
        follow = "--follow" in argv
        as_json = "--json" in argv
        if follow:
            while True:
                for note in b.inbox(session, mark=True, include_seen=include_seen):
                    print(b._note_line(note, session, b.now()), flush=True)
                include_seen = False
                b.sleep(2)
        notes = b.inbox(session, mark=not peek, include_seen=include_seen)
        if as_json:
            print(json.dumps(notes, sort_keys=True))
        elif notes:
            lines = [b._note_line(note, session, b.now()) for note in notes]
            hint = b._reply_hint(session, notes)
            if hint:
                lines.append(hint)
            print("\n".join(lines))
        return 0
    if cmd == "moor":
        writes = _opt(argv, "--writes")
        # _opt consumes the flag it reads, so each value is read exactly once.
        pid = _opt(argv, "--pid")
        ttl = _opt(argv, "--ttl")
        m = b.moor(session, model=_opt(argv, "--model"), lab=_opt(argv, "--lab"), runtime=_opt(argv, "--runtime"),
                   principal=_opt(argv, "--principal"), task=_opt(argv, "--task"),
                   writes=[w for w in writes.split(",") if w] if writes else None,
                   pid=int(pid) if pid else None,
                   ttl_s=int(ttl) if ttl else None)
        r = m["recipient"]
        print(f"moored {session} as {r.get('runtime', '?')} {r.get('model', '?')}@{r.get('lab', '?')} for {m.get('principal') or '?'}")
        return 0
    if cmd == "touch":
        pid = _opt(argv, "--pid")
        return 0 if b.touch(session, pid=int(pid) if pid else None) else 1
    if cmd == "unmoor":
        b.unmoor(session)
        print(f"unmoored {session}")
        failed = b.take_release_fold_failures()
        for res, why in failed:
            print(f"{res}: released here, but {why} — the other devices still see it held", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1 if failed else 0
    if cmd == "claim":
        res, note, ttl_s, klass, override, offline_ok, closure = claim_args
        # Claiming is a liveness act: a stale mooring would make the fresh lease look abandoned.
        if not b.touch(session):
            b.moor(session, pid=resolve_session_identity().get("ownerPid"))
        try:
            ok, lease, reason = b.claim(res, session, note=note, ttl_s=ttl_s, klass=klass,
                                        seat=os.environ.get("BERTH_SEAT") or None,
                                        override=override, session_source=source, offline_ok=offline_ok,
                                        closure=closure)
        except BerthUsage as e:
            print(f"berth: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if ok is None:
            print(f"{res}: {reason}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        if ok:
            head, _, tail = reason.partition("; ")
            print(f"{res}: {head} by {session} (session from {source})" + (f"\n  {tail}" if tail else ""))
            return 0
        if lease is None:
            print(f"{res}: REFUSED — {reason}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
        print(f"{res}: REFUSED — {reason}. Ask them, or wait; `berth say --to {getattr(lease, 'get', lambda k: None)('holder') if isinstance(lease, dict) else '<holder>'} …`",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    if cmd == "release":
        if not argv:
            print("usage: berth release RESOURCE --session S", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        force = "--force" in argv
        done = b.release(argv[0], session, force=force, reason="forced" if force else None)
        print(f"{argv[0]}: {'released' if done else 'was not held'} by {session}" + (" (forced)" if force and done else ""))
        failed = b.take_fold_failures(argv[0])
        if failed:
            print(f"{argv[0]}: released here, but {failed[0]} — the other devices still see it held",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        return 0
    if cmd == "say":
        to = _opt(argv, "--to")
        text = " ".join(argv).strip()
        if not text:
            print("usage: berth say --session S [--to SESSION] TEXT", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        b.say(session, text, to=to)
        failed = b.take_fold_failures(None)
        if failed:
            print(f"berth say: said here, but {failed[0]} — no other device will read it", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        return 0
    print(__doc__.split("Commands:")[1].split("Resources")[0])
    return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv))
